.TH "ROARK\-CREDENTIAL\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-credential-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-credential\-create \- Create a personal credential
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark credential create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Mints a credential that acts as you, for a CLI or an automation. The key value is returned exactly once, in the `key` field: capture it now, it is unreadable afterwards. Requires a personal credential (a project API key is refused) and admin on the project the credential defaults to. The new credential can never exceed the one that created it: not in scope, not in permissions, and not in lifetime. Omit a field to copy it from the calling credential.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/me/api\-keys
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
A label you will recognise later. It is the only thing that tells two credentials apart in the list you revoke from. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Project the credential assumes when a request sends no X\-Roark\-Project\-Id header. Defaults to the calling credential's own default project. You must be an admin of whichever project is used. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-scopes\fR \fI<value>\fR
Coarse tier. Defaults to the calling credential's own tier, and can never exceed it: a READ credential cannot mint a WRITE one. One of: READ, WRITE. Repeatable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-permissions\fR \fI<value>\fR
Granular 'resource:action' permissions. Defaults to the calling credential's own set, and can never exceed it. A ceiling, not an entitlement: the holder still only reaches what their project membership allows. Repeatable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\-at\fR \fI<value>\fR
ISO 8601 expiry. Defaults to the calling credential's own expiry (no expiry, for a `roark auth login` credential) and may not outlive it, so a short\-lived connector credential cannot mint a permanent one. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark credential create \-\-name <value>
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token used when \-\-token is not given.
.TP
\fBROARK_BASE_URL\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fBROARK_ALLOW_PROJECT_BASE_URL\fR
Trusts a base URL set by a project .roark.json, like \-\-allow\-project\-base\-url.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Disables colour when set to any value.
